{
 "schema": "dox-validate-benchmark-extension/1",
 "note": "Public documents added to the performance benchmark on 2026-11-15 to fill the page-count intervals that the frozen test corpus covers sparsely (it has one document with 11-19 pages and three to four in each interval from 20 to 999 pages). Never committed; bench/extension/fetch.py downloads them and checks each sha256. Selection, made from page count and publisher only, before any validator was run: candidates from the publishers of the test corpus (US federal agencies via their sites and govinfo, arXiv, LibreOffice) and German federal law (gesetze-im-internet.de); per interval documents were taken round-robin across publisher families, at most 3 per family, until the interval held 12 documents together with the test corpus; superseded editions were dropped. An exclusion check compared every sha256 with the sha256 list of the maintainers' internal dataset and with tests/corpus/public/manifest.json: no overlap. 'anchor' entries are documents of the frozen corpus measured again in the same run, to check that the two runs can be combined; they are copied from tests/corpus/.cache/full.",
